{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites","id":760666,"title":"[2ED] Your's Werewolf Rites","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-08T07:56:25-08:00","id":760666,"title":"[2ED] Your's Werewolf Rites","content":"Topic for your own, custom Rites to share.<br /> <br /> I start with mine Rite for <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/729981-regaining-auspice\">regaining Auspice</a> of ex Pure that want's to join Tribes of Moon.Thanks for help with this, <b>Deionscribe</b> and <b>Ephsy</b>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>Wolf Rite - Luna\u2019s Forgiveness (*****)</b><br /> <br /> Most Pure would rather die than return to the Mother\u2019s embrace. But in rare occasions there are dedicated Uratha that wish to regain their lost Auspice. This rite was used in this form since the first Pogrom, where early converts where begging Luna for her forgiveness. It's used to this night.<br /> <br /> This rite is taught only to the Tribes of Moon. Supplicant need to have at least one dot of his previous Auspice Renown.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Auspice's Moon, Forgiveness, Water, Auspice\u2019s Renown, Silver<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> The most common version of this ritual is performed on the night of the Auspice Moon convert wishes to regain. The ritualist summons a Lune of the Auspice in question which will send tales of the events of this night to the Moon. The supplicant begins by begging Luna for her forgiveness and the ritualist cleanses his body with water from silver basin that soaked the Moon\u2019s light. Then the gathering recreates the events of supplicant\u2019s First Change. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Other version:</b> The supplicant kneels at the bank of the river as the Auspice Moon rises in the night sky. The ritualist dips a silver chalice into the water, filling it up before holding it up to the sky to invoke the Lunar choir to act as witnesses to the rite. He then pours the water over the werewolf's head, as they and the other participants chant the First Tongue words of the Oath of the Moon. They, then, proceed to swim downriver, for the supplicant to prove his desire for forgiveness and the other participants to demonstrate their support for his cause&quot;. (Strength + Athletics)<br /> <br /> <b>Other version:</b> The rite's participants stand around the supplicant in a circle before a massive waterfall, its cascading waters glimmering under the light of the moon. The ritualist anoints the supplicant with body paint consecrated with powdered silver upon the scars of the rite which first tore away the Auspice's blessing. His assistants, meanwhile, intone a prayer in the First Tongue to Mother Luna, imploring her to look upon her lost child. Soon, a Lune of the Auspice's choir appears before the Uratha, speaking the words of the Oath before beckoning them to follow through the falls. The rite's other participants take turns affirming their support of the supplicant, before walking in a single line into the waterfall. The supplicant, himself, is the last to walk forward, and he braces himself for the full force of the water upon his body as he feels Essence flow through the paint and into his scars. (Stamina + Survival)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence and supplicant\u2019s 1 Primal Urge dot ( he cannot lose his/her first dot )<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Effect:</b> Supplicant regains his Auspice with it\u2019s spirit brands. He regains all Auspice abilities and reacts to the Auspice Moon like rest of Forsaken Uratha. The scars from the Pure ritual that stripped it previously fade with new flesh, but still are visible with a close inspection.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T10:22:29-08:00","id":776664,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mask the Blood (Wolf Rite, **)</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Sometimes the hunter becomes the hunted. A werewolf with this rite can mask their spiritual scent from their tireless hunters.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Symbols</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Scent, flight, stealth, blood</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Sample Rite</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A lone Iron Master living in Pure territory developed this rite over months of being hunted. He makes a fragrant broth out of onions, garlic, ammonia, and other materials with intense odor and anoints himself in the mixture. Afterwards, he bleeds into the container that he mixed the brew in and carries it far away from where he mixed it. Eventually he stops and conceals it. (Wits+Stealth)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action</b>:</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Extended (10 successes; each roll represents 5 minutes)</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Duration</b>: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Until another werewolf tastes of the ritualist\u2019s blood -- fresh or from the hidden container -- or 1 year.</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">: This rite can be performed by multiple werewolves simultaneously, and all can receive the benefit. Once successfully performed, all benefactors are protected from the werewolf ability to track a prey whose blood they\u2019ve tasted regardless of distance or time. Their spoor is once again \u201cmundane\u201d.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">This does not affect Facets such as Impossible Spoor or Honed Senses.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Rite I put together to justify the existence of a mentor character in my Cascadia Forsaken game. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":1923,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","user":"BigDamnHero","date":"as part of the sample rite. 11-29-2015, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:32:04-08:00","id":776693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites?p=776664#post776664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite I put together to justify the existence of a mentor character in my Cascadia Forsaken game. Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sample rite seems to be missing an evident symbolic correspondent to flight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T11:42:58-08:00","id":776701,"title":"","content":"Sounds legit to me. It's a lot like Cleanse the Blood from 1e so there's precedent as well. I'm not sure if the Flight symbol is necessarily represented in the rite itself, though the situation certainly. Unless the concealing of the jar is meant to represent that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T13:13:59-08:00","id":776767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites?p=776693#post776693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sample rite seems to be missing an evident symbolic correspondent to flight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meant to include part of the ritual wherein the ritemaster runs away with the container (the symbol is supposed to refer to the &quot;Fight or flight&quot; kind of flight).<br /> <br /> Fixed now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-27T23:20:27-08:00","id":818232,"title":"","content":"Here's something I'm trying to work out. A ritual devised by Egyptian and/or Mesopotamian Uratha of ancient times as an alternative to one created by the Nibiru (see LostLight's homebrew hub for more) to contain this <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/436971-new-idigam?p=818155#post818155\">monstrous Earthbound Idigam</a> that I thought up.<br /> <br /> If anyone's interested in helping me design this rite, I would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> -=-<br /> <br /> <u><b>Overcome the Serpent (ooo or ooooo)</b></u><br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Apep, Binding, Light, Purification<br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended<br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 Year<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T09:12:15-07:00","id":1209654,"title":"","content":"Rite I made for my games, using heavily Secondborns for Tribes structure.<br /> <br /> <b>Pack Rite - Call Secondborn (****)</b><br /> It\u2019s a Rite that summons <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1209584-are-there-secondborn\">Secondborn</a> \u2013 child wolf-spirit of Firstborn. It\u2019s often used for guidance or marking new Firstborn\u2019s Tribe members initiation with massager that will commune with Firstborn himself. Who, as not his spirit children, can watch out over day to day needs of Tribe under his power?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s more demanding version of ShadowCall (see WtF 2E p. 145 ) that summons named Firstborn child spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Wolf, Tribe, Firstborn Renown, Tribe\u2019s Sacred Prey<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> This is most popular version of rite<b>, </b>often use on Tribe new member initiation. Representation of wolf is circled by ritemaster and his helpers \u2013 it can be living wolf, but also can be only approximation, like stuffed or statue. Then Tribe members begin run for the place where locked is Tribe\u2019s Sacred Prey \u2013 dead or alive. The first of racers before touching Prey need to do action related to the Renown of Firstborn \u2013 and then take Prey to the place of representation of wolf. If rite is successful, Secondborn can Fetter to the representation and bless Tribe members. <b>( Strength + Athletics)</b><br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Extended (20 successes; each roll represents 1 minute); potentially contested by the spirit\u2019s Resistance<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> This rite targets a Secondborn, after calling his divine parent. The spirit becomes immediately aware once the rite begins, and can try to resist or can voluntarily respond to the call. If the rite succeeds, the spirit immediately appears within a delineated summoning spot that has appropriate Gathra in it. Unlike most rites, the local Gauntlet strength does affect the dice pool for Call Secondborn if the called spirit is on the opposite side of the Gauntlet to the ritemaster when the rite begins.<br /> <br /> If the summoning takes place in the material world, the area within the delineated space gains the Open Condition and the spirit appears in Twilight. If it has the Materialize Manifestation, then it may use this power at no cost when it appears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T04:16:38-07:00","id":1224131,"title":"","content":"<b>Pack Rite \u2013 Rite of Healing (***)</b><br /> <br /> Said to be most old of all Rites, being created in Pangea itself, it calls the powers of Shadow Realm to heal the wounds of those injured during hunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Water, Wolf, Cleansing, Healing<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>The most common version of this ritual is Rite Master that is cleansing the wounds of the target with fresh water, making new bandages. Pack then invoke various titles of the Wolf in First Tongue. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence per Aggravated wound healed + 1 per day of healings blessing per character<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 day per Essence spent<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Rite can be performed on many targets at ones. Rite heals instantly number of Aggravated wounds spent in Essence \u2013 but pool of them is shared between all targets of Rite, so for example 3 wounds in Essence can heal only 2 wounds of one character and 1 wound of the other. Then starts the blessing on each target \u2013 for numbers of days spent, character is healing like Uratha if not being one \u2013 or twice better if being Uratha. That means that Uratha character under blessing heals one Aggravated wound in two days and humans here Lethal wound each 15 minutes. In humans it leads to Integrity Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1923_4.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1923\" data-vbnamecard=\"1923\">BigDamnHero</a> , what do you think about it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-02-2018, 09:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T04:47:13-07:00","id":1224135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites?p=1224131#post1224131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pack Rite \u2013 Rote of Healing (***)</b><br /> <br /> Said to be most old of all Rites, being created in Pangea itself, it calls the powers of Shadow Realm to heal the wounds of those injured during hunt.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols:</b> Water, Wolf, Cleansing, Healing<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite: </b>The most common version of this ritual is Rite Master that is cleansing the wounds of the target with fresh water, making new bandages. Pack then invoke various titles of the Wolf in First Tongue. (Presence + Expression)<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 5 Essence per Aggravated wound healed + 1 per day of healings blessing per character<br /> <br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended ( 15 success, each roll represent 10 minutes )<br /> <br /> <b>Duration:</b> 1 day per Essence spent<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> Rite can be performed on many targets at ones. Rite heals instantly number of Aggravated wounds spent in Essence \u2013 but pool of them is shared between all targets of Rite, so for example 3 wounds in Essence can heal only 2 wounds of one character and 1 wound of the other. The stats the blessing on each target \u2013 for numbers of days spent, character is healing like Uratha if not being one \u2013 or twice better if being Uratha. That means that Uratha character under blessing heals one Aggravated wound in two days and humans here Lethal wound each 15 minutes. In humans it leads to Integrity Breaking Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather just summon and bind a spirit with the heal numina.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T05:12:00-07:00","id":1224138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites?p=1224135#post1224135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather just summon and bind a spirit with the heal numina.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would be difference? In <b>WtF </b>2E and <b>CoD </b>corebooks there is only <i>Regenerate </i>Numina, not <i>Heal</i> one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-02T06:22:04-07:00","id":1224146,"title":"","content":"Since when are you constrained only by what is printed in specific books, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T09:36:35-08:00","id":1268568,"title":"","content":"Saw this thread, kind of expected to see a bit more rites, but I think I'll add a few ones. These are taken from the <a href=\"https://wantonwicked.gamingsandbox.com/wiki/Werewolf/PlayerGuide#toc21\" target=\"_blank\">Wanton Wicked</a> custom rites and fetish wiki, just giving credit where it's due, left a link for it in case you want to check it out, there are few fetishes, there too.<br /> <br /> I added my own translation of the Hallow Touchstone rite, here you have it<br /> <br /> <b>Rite of the Essense Jar (\u2022\u2022, Wolf)</b><br /> <br /> In the hunt being stranded without essence might not be a direct death sentence but it surely makes life difficult for a werewolf and on top of that some gifts and numina can put a dent on a werewolves inner reserves, because of that shamans came up with this simple but ingenious rite. As the name suggest it creates a container for essence that can be carried on their person to have a bit extra juice available for whatever purpose without risking their inner reserves.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols</b><br /> Containers, Water, filling up the containers, The locus resonance<br /> <b>Sample Rite</b><br /> The Aegis pack makes use of a rite involving taking water in a bowl preparing it with some herbs , then taking glass bottles and inscribing sigils of protection on their surface while slowly filling them up with the previously prepared water(Wits+Occult)<br /> <b>Action </b>Extended (5 successes per recipient)<br /> <b>Duration</b> Month<br /> <b>Success</b><br /> Once the rite is finished each bottle starts to fill itself with the essence of the locus over the course of a day, one for each bottle, the essence matchs the locus resonance, each bottle can hold up to three essence points, but the rite can only make a number of bottles equal to the locus rating so a locus with a rating of 2 can only make two bottles. The uratha can \u201cdrink\u201d one essence per turn as an instant action, or drink the whole thing as a reflexive action but ony get one essence per bottle. Once a month has passed though, if the bottles have not been used, the essence is lost as it evaporates into the air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T04:40:12-08:00","id":1269180,"title":"","content":"I've littered quite a few new rites around the forum - just haven't gotten around to consolidating them all in one place!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T05:41:51-08:00","id":1274179,"title":"","content":"You know how the clothing adapts to werewolves when the changes shape?It adapts to Dalu size but it dissapears on gauru and the rest of the wolf forms, I was thinking of armor, Hishu and Dalu can wear it, but it's gone with the other three. I was thinking of translating the Dedicated Clothing rite to 2ed to take care of that. So gauru, urshul or urhan could benefit from mundane armory, though I suppose regular clothing could be used too, can't get the image out of my head of a werewolf in full gauru rage, wearing a business suit and biting someone heads off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-13T06:26:01-08:00","id":1274186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/760666-2ed-your-s-werewolf-rites?p=1274179#post1274179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know how the clothing adapts to werewolves when the changes shape?It adapts to Dalu size but it dissapears on gauru and the rest of the wolf forms, I was thinking of armor, Hishu and Dalu can wear it, but it's gone with the other three. I was thinking of translating the Dedicated Clothing rite to 2ed to take care of that. So gauru, urshul or urhan could benefit from mundane armory, though I suppose regular clothing could be used too, can't get the image out of my head of a werewolf in full gauru rage, wearing a business suit and biting someone heads off.</div> </div> </div> </div>I made a special <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1172668-2e-shapeshifting-armor-fetish?p=1172669#post1172669\">Fetish for the Shapeshifting Armors</a> - <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1172668-2e-shapeshifting-armor-fetish?p=1172669#post1172669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Shapeshifting Armor ( Fetish \u2022 - \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 )</b><br /> With Shapeshifting Armor Fetish Uratha ( or Wolf-Blooded with proper Tell ) can still get\u2019s all his normal Armor modifiers in his animal-based Forms ( Gauru, Urshul and Urhan ), that means modifiers for Armor Rating, Defense and Speed.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> Every witness that sees a character wearing this Fetish in their alternate forms <b><i>will remember and recognize the armor</i></b>, regardless of Form or result on the Lunacy check. Functionally this makes the armor a sort of Tell for those that would identify the wearer (As per Mortal Mask Numina). This is likely to affect Impression level for Social Manuevering, as appropriate.<br /> <b>Creation: </b>Shapeshifting Armor needs to lock the spirit of Rank equal to highest of two numbers \u2013 general Armor Rating or half of Ballistic Armor Rating of item, whichever is higher.</div> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T01:21:17-08:00","id":1274328,"title":"","content":"The drawback makes little sense. Armor is going to look like a similar theme in different forms, but &quot;remember and recognize the Armor&quot; seems unlikely. Especially ignoring Lunacy effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-14T07:07:22-08:00","id":1274360,"title":"","content":"wouldn't be better to say at higher levels of harmony (8 through 10) that it actively hurts for the armor to shift? maybe represented through penalty or 1 bashing damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-16T06:38:54-08:00","id":1274706,"title":"","content":"I agree, the drawback seems entirely unnecessary and makes no sense as it is, I would do away with it personally.<br /> <br /> Now making it a fetish I would just go straight to supernatural armor if it's a fetish that goes from 1 to 5 making it a scar fetish or tattoo, I would give a general 2 fetish rating, maybe 3 for a fetish on regular armor since it doesn't give the armor any supernatural traits other than shifting to fit the wolf forms to protect the body. Though an alternative with a 3 dot fetish you could modify the use of the Rage Glory facet to make it last a scene rather than just one attack.<br /> <br /> But this thread is for Rites which is why my suggestion was a translation of the dedicated clothing rite from 1ed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24813,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","user":"Aeveth","date":". 12-16-2018, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-17T12:40:11-07:00","id":1297559,"title":"","content":"<b>Rite of the Battle Brand (Pack, \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Blood Talon Rite</b><br /> A pack of howling, snarling Uratha wearing the war form and charging out of the darkness with Rage in their eyes is an intimidating sight. Most any<br /> human, and more than a few of the supernatural denizens of the World of Darkness, would flee in abject terror at such a vision of death bearing down on them. But when the natural intimidation factor of a werewolf\u2019s Rage isn\u2019t enough, the Blood Talons employ this rite, to pump themselves up before a battle and to intimidate their foes.<br /> <br /> Although many Blood Talon ritualists agree that the Rite of the Battle Brand is an original creation of their tribe, this rite has a bad reputation in some areas contested by the Pure. The imagery of the ritual is undeniably similar to that used in the rites of the Fire-Touched, and the Izidakh are known to employ similar pre-battle rituals. Whether this is a case of parallel evolution or one tribe appropriating the rituals of their enemies, ritualists are advised to step lightly when performing this rite in territories where war against the Anshega is common.<br /> <br /> <b>Sample Rite:</b> On the eve of battle, the ritualist and any participating werewolves gather in a large, open space and build a fire. This could be anything from an inferno in a clearing in the woods to a burning trash can in an empty parking lot, as long as the fire is at least bonfire-sized.<br /> <br /> Once the fire is banked up to its full intensity, the werewolves begin to circle around it, moving in a stuttering, uneven counterclockwise loop. As the shadows dance and flicker, the pack members change shape at random, striving to match their changes to the shifting firelight. The ritualist stands in the center of the ring next to the bonfire and shouts exhortations to Glory and Honor in battle. The ritual often takes a call-and-response form, with the ritualist bellowing a challenge that the participants answer with shouts, roars or howls.<br /> <br /> Finally, when the assembled werewolves are judged to be suitably worked up, the ritualist calls each forward in turn and sears him with a brand from the fire. The brand is usually made on the chest or arm, but some Blood Talons prefer to mark themselves on the brow. The brand inflicts a minimum of one point of lethal damage, but it is considered a point of pride to wear a more severe brand into battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Presence+Expression<br /> <b>Action: </b>Extended (5 Success needed per bonus dice, each roll takes 1 minute)<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Until Sunrise<br /> <b>Effect:</b> Once the rite is completed, the pack and the ritemaster receieve a bonus to attacks depending on how many successes where allocated to the rite, +1 if only 5, up to +5 bonus wth 25 successes, furthermore, compare the bonus recieved against any attacker Composure, the difference counts as a penalty to attack the werewolf blessed by this rite.<br /> <br /> Taken from Tribes of The Moon pg. 42, had to modify it a little but kept most of it unchanged","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}